Z||000004||DecadenceR||06-19-2001||02:11 PM||||But Greg, do you actually HAVE this stuff on your car?<BR>Loko at the stickers I told you about. First this guy has 2 different kinds of tire scikers on his car, for tires he doesn't even have! Second, I'd say there's a possibility of maybe 2 of thos eother things actually being in his car, since it was quiet, slow, and by all outer apperances stock!!!<BR>I have no poblem with stickers on a car, but at least use what you have tehs tickers for!!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Greg Piet||06-19-2001||02:43 PM||||First off I really dont care whether my car is rice or not...  I like it the way it is and to heck with everyone else.<P>I am just trying to defend the owner of the white sticker laden Fiero by mentioning my car which typically people do not call rice, just in bad need of a paint job.<P>I have not dyno tested it yet but its a lot stronger than any 2.8 I ever was in(especially in the 3000RPM plus range).<P>My powered by pontiac sticker has been transformed into a Pontiac Racing hat.<P>I have Hoosier and Kumho stickers on my car, and I dont use Hoosiers or Kumhos unless I am on the track and never at the same time. But there is a set of both Kumho V700's and Hoosier A3S03's in my garage next to my tire trailer.<P>I am also curious how one tells from the outside of a moving car whether it is an automatic or a stick shift (I cannot do that).<P>From the topic starter it appears that this white Fiero is rice by its stickers and stock appearance...  by that my car is rice as well... <P>I also have been known to be slow according to other cars driving around town.  If it is blatently obvious that the other car is a joke I dont even bother...  Then there is also the case where I just want to casually tool around town.<P>I imagine The purple pavement eater driver would not even bother with going fast in front of my car as it is such a wimpy car. <P>Lets see if I get this right<BR>momo=steering wheel<BR>msd=ignition box<BR>accel=wires or ign module in distributor<BR>hooker=rollbar or header<BR>pacesetter=header or ?swaybar?<BR>hks= ok i dont know this but I am guessing suspension/shocks<BR>borla=muffler<BR>nitto=tire <BR>pirelli=tire||||reg||1
Z||000006||1FST2M6||06-19-2001||04:08 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.hksusa.com" TARGET=_blank>www.hksusa.com</A>  I had HKS parts on the SE and some on the GT... (intkae fittings, and better then Aeroquip AN fittings (not aluminum Titanium/nitrile o-rings) but 90% of the cars you see with HKS stickers and such are just frontin' and most are rice... I'm runnin Apex-i parts on the GT now too...   <P>why advertise for somthing if your not making $ off it or unless they gave you somthing for free. <P>just my $.02 ||||reg||1
Z||000007||cadaver||06-19-2001||05:04 PM||||Better than Aeroquip? I doubt that maybe more expensive.||||reg||1
